1
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:09,360
Do you like Yok?

2
00:00:12,480 --> 00:00:14,640
That face of yours doesn't just belong to you.

3
00:00:14,760 --> 00:00:16,680
It carries the name of the Sukonsiri family.

4
00:00:16,960 --> 00:00:19,000
Isn't he supposed to be handling this project?

5
00:00:19,760 --> 00:00:22,480
Yes, but he's currently on leave.

6
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:24,160
Let go of me.

7
00:00:25,560 --> 00:00:26,360
Why?

8
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:28,520
You have no right to touch her shares.

9
00:00:31,640 --> 00:00:34,680
Why won't you just give up on this already?

10
00:00:43,640 --> 00:00:44,840
What on earth am I wearing?

11
00:00:45,080 --> 00:00:46,760
Is this the best shirt you could find?

12
00:00:47,400 --> 00:00:48,440
Just wear it.

13
00:00:50,480 --> 00:00:51,080
No way.

14
00:00:51,640 --> 00:00:54,520
I'm going to give you a fashion lesson sometime, okay?

15
00:00:59,440 --> 00:01:00,600
I'm leaving.

16
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:02,600
Where are you going?

17
00:01:03,280 --> 00:01:04,319
Who said you could leave?

18
00:01:05,480 --> 00:01:07,240
Now, get in the car.

19
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:09,480
Tomorrow's a day off.

20
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:11,160
You have to keep me company.

21
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:12,960
Will you?

22
00:01:13,680 --> 00:01:14,640
Come on, get in.

23
00:01:16,240 --> 00:01:17,200
Get in the car.

24
00:01:18,520 --> 00:01:19,360
Fine.

25
00:01:21,360 --> 00:01:22,280
P'Ing...

26
00:01:27,600 --> 00:01:28,800
Make me something to eat, too.

27
00:03:53,120 --> 00:03:54,600
I'm hungry.

28
00:03:54,680 --> 00:03:57,720
I'm so hungry and exhausted.

29
00:03:58,800 --> 00:04:00,240
Want me to whip something up for you?

30
00:04:00,280 --> 00:04:00,960
Yes.

31
00:04:03,560 --> 00:04:05,400
What are you going to make?

32
00:04:05,440 --> 00:04:06,360
Give me a second.

33
00:04:06,400 --> 00:04:08,040
What are you making?

34
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:13,000
What do you want to eat?

35
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:18,959
Let's check the fridge.

36
00:04:25,120 --> 00:04:26,120
There's nothing in here.

37
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:29,640
Just go get some rest.

38
00:04:29,640 --> 00:04:30,720
I'll handle it.

39
00:04:32,760 --> 00:04:33,960
You're so sweet.

40
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:35,800
I'll be waiting for it.

41
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:35,720
P'Ing.

42
00:05:37,159 --> 00:05:39,240
P'Ing, wake up and eat.

43
00:05:39,880 --> 00:05:41,280
No, I'm sleepy.

44
00:05:45,320 --> 00:05:46,960
Get up right now.

45
00:05:51,640 --> 00:05:53,040
Eat your food.

46
00:05:53,400 --> 00:05:54,560
Fine.

47
00:05:54,600 --> 00:05:55,840
Sit up, come on.

48
00:05:55,920 --> 00:05:56,560
I'll eat.

49
00:05:57,400 --> 00:05:58,159
I'll eat...

50
00:06:00,680 --> 00:06:01,720
I'll eat my food.

51
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:07,960
Where is it?

52
00:06:09,600 --> 00:06:10,640
Feed me first.

53
00:06:21,800 --> 00:06:23,720
You're so sweet. Even blew on it for me?

54
00:06:37,280 --> 00:06:38,280
This is actually good.

55
00:06:39,960 --> 00:06:40,800
You're good at pampering me,

56
00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:41,960
and you're a great cook.

57
00:06:42,400 --> 00:06:43,960
Now you're finally acting like a bottom.

58
00:06:45,520 --> 00:06:46,560
Who's your bottom?

59
00:06:47,920 --> 00:06:48,720
I'm your top.

60
00:07:14,880 --> 00:07:16,560
Your cooking is really something.

61
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:18,720
It's nothing special.

62
00:07:18,760 --> 00:07:21,280
Tell me. Who else have you cooked for?

63
00:07:21,560 --> 00:07:23,840
I just cook for myself at the dorm.

64
00:07:27,400 --> 00:07:28,840
Now that's a great answer.

65
00:07:28,840 --> 00:07:29,640
Alright.

66
00:07:32,640 --> 00:07:33,760
I'll give you a little reward.

67
00:07:40,600 --> 00:07:41,560
Your mom?

68
00:07:45,240 --> 00:07:46,240
Hello, Mom.

69
00:07:47,680 --> 00:07:49,600
Yok, it's already 9:30.

70
00:07:49,640 --> 00:07:50,920
Are you coming home soon?

71
00:07:51,640 --> 00:07:53,320
I made some chicken soup.

72
00:07:53,360 --> 00:07:54,560
It's still nice and warm.

73
00:07:54,560 --> 00:07:57,000
I have something to take care of at the college.

74
00:07:57,560 --> 00:07:59,440
I won't be able to come home for a few days.

75
00:08:03,520 --> 00:08:05,720
Hello, ma'am. It's me.

76
00:08:06,440 --> 00:08:07,080
Yes.

77
00:08:07,560 --> 00:08:09,520
I'm the one Yok is interning with.

78
00:08:10,760 --> 00:08:12,080
The thing is...

79
00:08:12,600 --> 00:08:14,880
something came up at my company,

80
00:08:14,960 --> 00:08:16,880
so I really need Yok's help.

81
00:08:16,920 --> 00:08:17,920
I'm very sorry, ma'am,

82
00:08:17,960 --> 00:08:20,560
but I'll need to borrow Yok for a couple of days.

83
00:08:21,320 --> 00:08:23,160
I'll take excellent care of him.

84
00:08:23,200 --> 00:08:25,080
I won't let a single ant anywhere near him.

85
00:08:25,800 --> 00:08:27,000
Oh...

86
00:08:27,720 --> 00:08:30,720
Ma'am, please talk to Yok again.

87
00:08:33,320 --> 00:08:34,280
Hello, Mom?

88
00:08:34,280 --> 00:08:35,440
Go ahead and focus on work.

89
00:08:35,480 --> 00:08:38,080
If you need anything, just call me anytime.

90
00:08:38,120 --> 00:08:40,039
Get some sleep, Mom. Good night.

91
00:08:43,039 --> 00:08:44,440
Are you out of your mind, P'Ing?

92
00:08:44,840 --> 00:08:45,840
I'm not.

93
00:08:45,880 --> 00:08:47,200
What's wrong with you?

94
00:08:47,240 --> 00:08:48,800
You can't even pick out your own shirt.

95
00:08:48,800 --> 00:08:50,440
Not everyone can be such a pro like you.

96
00:08:50,960 --> 00:08:52,120
But at least...

97
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:55,280
I don't lie to you.

98
00:08:56,360 --> 00:08:58,080
You're all talk, P'Ing.

99
00:08:58,520 --> 00:09:00,280
I'm not all talk. My mouth has other skills, too.

100
00:09:01,120 --> 00:09:02,200
Can you handle this?

101
00:09:07,480 --> 00:09:08,480
Can you take it?

102
00:09:11,080 --> 00:09:12,200
Should we go to the sink?

103
00:09:12,800 --> 00:09:13,520
I'd prefer the couch.

104
00:09:42,520 --> 00:09:44,120
It has been nearly a month

105
00:09:44,160 --> 00:09:45,720
since Thailand entered the rainy season.

106
00:09:45,760 --> 00:09:46,200
Bangkok,

107
00:09:46,240 --> 00:09:46,840
the metropolitan areas,

108
00:09:46,840 --> 00:09:48,720
and most parts of Central Thailand

109
00:09:48,840 --> 00:09:50,160
remain under the influence

110
00:09:50,160 --> 00:09:52,360
of the southwest monsoon,

111
00:09:52,400 --> 00:09:54,280
causing humidity levels

112
00:09:54,280 --> 00:09:56,120
to remain consistently high.

113
00:09:56,160 --> 00:09:57,640
The public is advised

114
00:09:57,680 --> 00:09:59,600
to closely monitor weather forecasts

115
00:09:59,640 --> 00:10:00,680
and take precautions

116
00:10:00,720 --> 00:10:02,400
against changing weather.

117
00:10:10,920 --> 00:10:12,320
Happy Birthday.

118
00:10:12,320 --> 00:10:13,720
Make a wish before you blow out the candles.

119
00:10:32,800 --> 00:10:36,160
After months of rain, the rainy season has finally ended.

120
00:10:36,200 --> 00:10:37,400
Cold winds from the north

121
00:10:37,400 --> 00:10:38,840
are reaching Bangkok,

122
00:10:38,880 --> 00:10:39,680
the metropolitan areas,

123
00:10:39,720 --> 00:10:40,960
and Central Thailand.

124
00:10:40,960 --> 00:10:42,480
Where did you get all this energy?

125
00:10:42,520 --> 00:10:44,800
The skies are beginning to clear

126
00:10:44,840 --> 00:10:46,520
as the gentle morning sunshine

127
00:10:46,560 --> 00:10:49,240
and cool winds offer a break

128
00:10:49,280 --> 00:10:51,520
from the heat of the rainy season.

129
00:10:51,560 --> 00:10:53,960
The most pleasant time of the year

130
00:10:53,960 --> 00:10:55,440
has begun once again.

131
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:56,960
Here, have some more.

132
00:10:57,000 --> 00:10:59,240
Alright, come on.

133
00:10:59,280 --> 00:11:01,000
-That's enough. -Keep it coming.

134
00:11:01,840 --> 00:11:03,040
-Cheers? -He's here.

135
00:11:03,920 --> 00:11:05,080
Hey, Ing.

136
00:11:05,840 --> 00:11:06,920
Over here.

137
00:11:07,640 --> 00:11:08,320
What's up?

138
00:11:08,720 --> 00:11:10,680
Look who finally showed up.

139
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:15,000
Have you guys been here long?

140
00:11:15,160 --> 00:11:16,400
For a while now.

141
00:11:16,520 --> 00:11:18,560
Man, took you long enough to get here.

142
00:11:20,320 --> 00:11:21,320
And who's this?

143
00:11:22,960 --> 00:11:24,480
This is Yok, Phet's younger brother.

144
00:11:24,840 --> 00:11:27,600
I see.

145
00:11:28,520 --> 00:11:29,840
The one you're always talking about?

146
00:11:29,840 --> 00:11:30,560
Yeah.

147
00:11:31,040 --> 00:11:32,520
Finally getting to meet him in person.

148
00:11:32,560 --> 00:11:35,200
Wow, he's way more handsome than you made him out to be.

149
00:11:35,240 --> 00:11:36,800
He's interning with me right now.

150
00:11:39,520 --> 00:11:41,080
Feel free to give him some pointers.

151
00:11:45,200 --> 00:11:47,080
Make sure they're the good kind of pointers, though.

152
00:11:47,520 --> 00:11:48,360
With you mentoring him,

153
00:11:48,400 --> 00:11:49,800
does he even need us?

154
00:11:50,080 --> 00:11:50,800
Right?

155
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:52,400
There's nothing left for us to teach him.

156
00:11:52,400 --> 00:11:53,120
Yeah.

157
00:11:53,160 --> 00:11:55,040
Especially if it's advice from you.

158
00:11:55,080 --> 00:11:56,640
Let's introduce ourselves.

159
00:11:56,680 --> 00:11:58,080
Pleased to meet you.

160
00:11:58,440 --> 00:11:59,480
My name is Leo.

161
00:12:00,800 --> 00:12:02,200
Hello, P'Leo.

162
00:12:04,960 --> 00:12:06,560
I'm in business, too,

163
00:12:06,920 --> 00:12:09,120
and I'm opening a new restaurant.

164
00:12:09,640 --> 00:12:12,280
Usually, Ing doesn't take anyone under his wing.

165
00:12:12,560 --> 00:12:14,520
That means you must be pretty special.

166
00:12:16,800 --> 00:12:18,400
He's definitely something else.

167
00:12:18,880 --> 00:12:20,600
He is special. Don't you agree?

168
00:12:23,960 --> 00:12:25,360
I'm going to the bathroom.

169
00:12:31,200 --> 00:12:32,240
It's nothing.

170
00:12:33,080 --> 00:12:34,360
He's just nervous.

171
00:12:34,360 --> 00:12:35,360
Give him some time.

172
00:12:54,120 --> 00:12:55,600
Why do you look so upset with me tonight?

173
00:12:57,320 --> 00:12:58,000
P'Ing,

174
00:12:58,360 --> 00:12:59,800
don't tell your friends about us again.

175
00:12:59,800 --> 00:13:00,560
What are you talking about?

176
00:13:01,960 --> 00:13:02,760
Oh...

177
00:13:03,320 --> 00:13:04,120
Why?

178
00:13:04,600 --> 00:13:06,520
I just wanted you to know my friends.

179
00:13:07,280 --> 00:13:08,280
I didn't mean anything by it.

180
00:13:08,800 --> 00:13:10,360
Can you stop overthinking things?

181
00:13:12,320 --> 00:13:13,040
Yok,

182
00:13:13,280 --> 00:13:15,200
I'm a straightforward guy.

183
00:13:15,880 --> 00:13:17,160
If you don't believe me, fine.

184
00:13:22,200 --> 00:13:23,160
It's getting late.

185
00:13:24,240 --> 00:13:25,320
I'll drive you home.

186
00:13:25,600 --> 00:13:26,840
I don't have any other plans.

187
00:13:27,360 --> 00:13:28,400
I'll keep you company.

188
00:13:36,840 --> 00:13:37,960
Listen carefully.

189
00:13:38,320 --> 00:13:39,560
I don't need anyone

190
00:13:39,600 --> 00:13:41,360
to pity me.

191
00:13:41,960 --> 00:13:42,920
And let me tell you this,

192
00:13:42,960 --> 00:13:44,200
it won't be long before I make you

193
00:13:44,240 --> 00:13:45,520
want to be mine.

194
00:13:48,880 --> 00:13:50,040
You don't need to give me a ride.

195
00:13:51,720 --> 00:13:52,680
I can go home by myself.

196
00:14:27,520 --> 00:14:28,720
Hey, not bad.

197
00:14:29,040 --> 00:14:30,760
Go on, get some water.

198
00:14:39,320 --> 00:14:39,800
[P'Ing,]

199
00:14:39,840 --> 00:14:41,240
[didn't you want me to teach you how to box?]

200
00:14:41,240 --> 00:14:42,600
[I'll be at the boxing gym all day tomorrow.]

201
00:14:42,600 --> 00:14:43,600
[Are you coming?]

202
00:14:43,600 --> 00:14:45,280
Hey, look at our future champ.

203
00:14:45,280 --> 00:14:46,920
What's so interesting on that phone?

204
00:14:50,640 --> 00:14:53,200
The results for the tryout round are coming out soon.

205
00:14:53,600 --> 00:14:54,720
Don't let me down.

206
00:14:56,040 --> 00:14:56,720
I won't.

207
00:15:09,240 --> 00:15:09,840
Good.

208
00:15:12,240 --> 00:15:13,040
Great.

209
00:15:18,280 --> 00:15:18,960
Yok...

210
00:15:20,600 --> 00:15:21,800
Your mind is wandering.

211
00:15:22,520 --> 00:15:23,600
You're losing focus.

212
00:15:24,080 --> 00:15:25,360
This isn't the first time.

213
00:15:25,840 --> 00:15:27,720
You know what the worst reason

214
00:15:27,760 --> 00:15:28,960
for a boxer to lose is?

215
00:15:29,920 --> 00:15:31,880
Because their mind is distracted.

216
00:15:36,800 --> 00:15:37,880
I'm sorry, P'Khun.

217
00:15:52,480 --> 00:15:54,480
Hello.

218
00:15:59,720 --> 00:16:00,480
Do I look good?

219
00:16:05,160 --> 00:16:06,320
It suits you well.

220
00:16:07,480 --> 00:16:09,200
Since I've come all this way,

221
00:16:09,200 --> 00:16:10,920
please take good care of me.

222
00:16:13,040 --> 00:16:15,720
Then let's start by warming up.

223
00:16:17,880 --> 00:16:19,640
Why so cold?

224
00:16:19,800 --> 00:16:21,880
You can't become good at boxing overnight.

225
00:16:22,280 --> 00:16:23,680
Since you said you wanted to learn,

226
00:16:24,160 --> 00:16:25,520
I have to take the training seriously.

227
00:16:26,880 --> 00:16:28,040
Keeping it cool, huh?

228
00:16:28,640 --> 00:16:29,840
I'll wait and see

229
00:16:29,880 --> 00:16:31,040
how good you really are.

230
00:16:38,400 --> 00:16:40,080
Drive the power from your hips.

231
00:16:40,120 --> 00:16:40,600
Like this?

232
00:16:40,640 --> 00:16:41,760
No, twist.

233
00:16:42,080 --> 00:16:43,160
-Twist upward. -Like this?

234
00:16:43,200 --> 00:16:44,160
-Twist. -Twist upward?

235
00:16:44,680 --> 00:16:45,360
Like this?

236
00:16:46,880 --> 00:16:47,480
P'Ing.

237
00:16:48,920 --> 00:16:49,960
Do you actually want to learn?

238
00:16:51,600 --> 00:16:52,200
I do.

239
00:16:53,560 --> 00:16:54,960
I'm being serious here.

240
00:16:57,600 --> 00:16:58,280
Is this alright?

241
00:17:00,200 --> 00:17:00,800
Do you want to learn?

242
00:17:00,800 --> 00:17:01,720
Yes, I am learning here.

243
00:17:04,760 --> 00:17:05,800
Now, twist your hips.

244
00:17:07,040 --> 00:17:07,599
That's it.

245
00:17:10,280 --> 00:17:11,160
That's correct.

246
00:17:11,200 --> 00:17:12,079
Is it too tight?

247
00:17:12,119 --> 00:17:12,920
It's just right.

248
00:17:13,680 --> 00:17:14,480
Okay.

249
00:17:15,400 --> 00:17:16,440
Stay still.

250
00:17:20,119 --> 00:17:21,800
Once you're finished, wrap it around the wrist.

251
00:17:23,440 --> 00:17:24,480
Do you remember any of this?

252
00:17:25,160 --> 00:17:26,440
No, it happened too fast.

253
00:17:27,520 --> 00:17:29,720
P'Ing, you have to do it properly.

254
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:31,160
Otherwise, you might get hurt.

255
00:17:31,760 --> 00:17:32,680
Are you worried about me?

256
00:17:34,600 --> 00:17:35,720
There's no need for me to remember.

257
00:17:36,080 --> 00:17:37,320
Whenever I want to box,

258
00:17:37,360 --> 00:17:39,040
I'll just have you wrap them for me.

259
00:17:40,360 --> 00:17:41,960
Will I be with you all the time?

260
00:17:41,960 --> 00:17:42,480
Yes.

261
00:17:42,840 --> 00:17:43,640
Can't you?

262
00:17:47,080 --> 00:17:47,880
Stop smiling.

263
00:17:48,520 --> 00:17:49,720
Just admit it if you want to be with me.

264
00:17:50,240 --> 00:17:51,400
Here, the other hand.

265
00:17:54,360 --> 00:17:55,160
P'Ing.

266
00:17:55,640 --> 00:17:56,280
Do it right.

267
00:17:56,280 --> 00:17:57,240
Use your shoulders

268
00:17:57,280 --> 00:17:58,120
and twist your waist.

269
00:18:00,720 --> 00:18:02,360
Have you ever boxed before?

270
00:18:02,400 --> 00:18:03,360
I'm just a natural.

271
00:18:03,400 --> 00:18:05,280
Then let's go for another hundred punches.

272
00:18:05,840 --> 00:18:06,880
My punches are powerful, though.

273
00:18:11,040 --> 00:18:12,240
Hey, Yok.

274
00:18:13,080 --> 00:18:14,400
-Does it hurt a lot? -Ouch.

275
00:18:17,160 --> 00:18:18,320
-Just kidding. -I... Hey.

276
00:18:22,120 --> 00:18:23,440
Stop it. That tickles.

277
00:18:23,480 --> 00:18:24,720
Once I get up...

278
00:18:24,920 --> 00:18:25,560
Yok.

279
00:18:28,400 --> 00:18:29,320
Right here?

280
00:18:30,960 --> 00:18:31,960
Teach me now.

281
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:32,680
P'Ing.

282
00:18:32,680 --> 00:18:33,840
Come on, teach me.

283
00:18:34,120 --> 00:18:34,920
Stop.

284
00:18:35,240 --> 00:18:36,040
Stop it.

285
00:18:36,560 --> 00:18:37,320
Teasing me, huh?

286
00:18:37,520 --> 00:18:38,280
Stop.

287
00:18:50,480 --> 00:18:51,240
Yok.

288
00:18:53,080 --> 00:18:53,920
Come sit over here.

289
00:18:54,360 --> 00:18:54,960
Okay.

290
00:19:02,440 --> 00:19:03,720
Why do you like boxing so much?

291
00:19:06,640 --> 00:19:07,920
Whenever I'm boxing,

292
00:19:10,280 --> 00:19:12,080
all my problems just seem to vanish.

293
00:19:13,720 --> 00:19:15,120
Everything becomes so simple.

294
00:19:16,440 --> 00:19:17,320
There's only punching,

295
00:19:18,560 --> 00:19:19,360
losing,

296
00:19:19,960 --> 00:19:20,880
or winning.

297
00:19:24,840 --> 00:19:25,640
Hold on,

298
00:19:27,040 --> 00:19:28,160
how is that even simple?

299
00:19:29,920 --> 00:19:31,320
You wouldn't understand.

300
00:19:35,760 --> 00:19:36,360
Look.

301
00:19:38,960 --> 00:19:39,920
Maybe sometimes,

302
00:19:40,920 --> 00:19:42,040
you're just making things

303
00:19:42,080 --> 00:19:43,320
more complicated than they need to be.

304
00:19:52,480 --> 00:19:54,280
Not everyone's like you,

305
00:19:55,880 --> 00:19:57,880
just acting on whatever they're thinking.

306
00:20:00,200 --> 00:20:02,240
Thinking things through is all well and good,

307
00:20:03,560 --> 00:20:05,280
but keeping it all bottled up isn't healthy.

308
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:09,080
If you ever need to let it all out,

309
00:20:10,920 --> 00:20:12,040
I'm right here for you.

310
00:20:28,200 --> 00:20:29,760
This place is actually pretty chill,

311
00:20:29,760 --> 00:20:30,440
isn't it?

312
00:20:34,240 --> 00:20:35,080
Hey,

313
00:20:38,280 --> 00:20:39,680
aren't you crossing the line?

314
00:20:40,600 --> 00:20:41,520
Give me that cigarette.

315
00:20:42,280 --> 00:20:43,520
One, two, three.

316
00:20:43,560 --> 00:20:45,000
Smoking is bad for you.

317
00:20:47,920 --> 00:20:49,080
Caught me off guard, huh?

318
00:20:49,960 --> 00:20:51,080
If you're really that good,

319
00:20:52,680 --> 00:20:54,320
try to take this lighter from me.

320
00:21:05,640 --> 00:21:06,320
Whoa.

321
00:21:07,200 --> 00:21:08,080
How did you do that?

322
00:21:09,160 --> 00:21:09,920
Teach me.

323
00:21:10,400 --> 00:21:11,080
That was cool.

324
00:21:11,360 --> 00:21:12,480
Show me how to do it.

325
00:21:12,560 --> 00:21:13,400
How do I do that?

326
00:21:13,440 --> 00:21:14,240
How?

327
00:21:14,920 --> 00:21:15,680
How do I do it?

328
00:21:16,120 --> 00:21:16,880
Like this?

329
00:21:17,800 --> 00:21:18,920
Teach me.

330
00:21:18,960 --> 00:21:19,960
Hold my wrist.

331
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:21,720
Hold it like this?

332
00:21:21,720 --> 00:21:22,840
Oh, like this?

333
00:21:22,880 --> 00:21:23,880
No, use the other hand.

334
00:21:23,920 --> 00:21:24,680
This hand...

335
00:21:27,120 --> 00:21:27,720
Ow...

336
00:21:30,840 --> 00:21:31,400
P'Ing.

337
00:21:31,440 --> 00:21:32,400
Are you alright?

338
00:21:32,440 --> 00:21:33,480
Did you do that on purpose?

339
00:21:33,520 --> 00:21:35,560
No, it just happened.

340
00:21:35,560 --> 00:21:36,560
My bad.

341
00:21:37,560 --> 00:21:38,920
Aw...

342
00:21:39,360 --> 00:21:40,480
How about this?

343
00:21:41,280 --> 00:21:42,960
If you can last a day without smoking,

344
00:21:43,400 --> 00:21:44,880
I'll keep you company tomorrow.

345
00:22:03,600 --> 00:22:04,520
Hello, Auntie.

346
00:22:04,720 --> 00:22:07,040
Hi, Ing. It's me.

347
00:22:07,120 --> 00:22:08,760
I'm calling to congratulate you, Ing.

348
00:22:09,160 --> 00:22:10,640
I heard the new condo

349
00:22:10,640 --> 00:22:12,760
is selling like hotcakes, right?

350
00:22:12,800 --> 00:22:14,000
Thank you.

351
00:22:14,280 --> 00:22:16,720
Actually, I wanted to ask you about something.

352
00:22:17,120 --> 00:22:19,080
I heard you're planning to set aside

353
00:22:19,080 --> 00:22:21,040
a few units for Director Pha-nu.

354
00:22:21,480 --> 00:22:25,360
Could you have Pite handle this instead?

355
00:22:30,040 --> 00:22:31,600
I'll have to see what everyone says

356
00:22:31,640 --> 00:22:33,120
in the meeting first.

357
00:22:33,960 --> 00:22:35,720
Alright. Goodbye.

358
00:22:41,200 --> 00:22:42,400
Dammit.

359
00:22:42,960 --> 00:22:44,600
How did Pite even know about this?

360
00:22:46,080 --> 00:22:46,920
Come in.

361
00:22:47,840 --> 00:22:48,800
How did Pite know

362
00:22:48,840 --> 00:22:50,560
we were securing units for Director Pha-nu?

363
00:22:50,600 --> 00:22:51,920
His mom just called me,

364
00:22:52,160 --> 00:22:54,080
begging me to let him in on the deal.

365
00:22:54,200 --> 00:22:55,200
I already told you

366
00:22:55,200 --> 00:22:56,240
to keep this under wraps.

367
00:22:56,240 --> 00:22:57,520
More people knowing means more risk.

368
00:22:57,800 --> 00:22:59,480
P'Ing, that day,

369
00:22:59,480 --> 00:23:01,720
he insisted on taking me out to eat,

370
00:23:01,760 --> 00:23:03,280
and when I went to the bathroom,

371
00:23:03,320 --> 00:23:04,480
he snooped through my documents.

372
00:23:04,520 --> 00:23:05,480
Then why did you leave

373
00:23:05,520 --> 00:23:06,600
sensitive documents lying around?

374
00:23:06,920 --> 00:23:08,680
I didn't think he'd snoop through them.

375
00:23:08,720 --> 00:23:09,480
When I got back,

376
00:23:09,480 --> 00:23:10,520
he asked me if the documents

377
00:23:10,560 --> 00:23:12,320
were meant for Director Pha-nu.

378
00:23:12,360 --> 00:23:13,680
I didn't give him an answer,

379
00:23:13,680 --> 00:23:14,840
but he assumed I was confirming it.

380
00:23:14,840 --> 00:23:16,160
Then he added that...

381
00:23:16,360 --> 00:23:18,240
the land for the hotel his mom is working on

382
00:23:18,280 --> 00:23:20,280
needs Director Pha-nu's approval as well.

383
00:23:20,760 --> 00:23:23,080
I think he's trying to use this opportunity

384
00:23:23,120 --> 00:23:24,760
to expand his connections.

385
00:23:24,920 --> 00:23:25,960
That jerk...

386
00:23:26,640 --> 00:23:28,000
I have to hand it to him.

387
00:23:28,040 --> 00:23:30,280
At least he's getting smarter.

388
00:23:30,800 --> 00:23:32,360
Instead of looking for business outside,

389
00:23:32,720 --> 00:23:34,000
he's decided to prey on his own family.

390
00:23:34,040 --> 00:23:34,840
How did he come up with that?

391
00:23:35,160 --> 00:23:37,840
P'Ing, what should I do?

392
00:23:38,200 --> 00:23:39,520
Tell me what you want me to do.

393
00:23:39,560 --> 00:23:40,720
I caused this mess,

394
00:23:40,760 --> 00:23:41,920
so I'll make it right.

395
00:23:43,120 --> 00:23:45,160
At least you're owning up to it.

396
00:23:45,160 --> 00:23:47,080
From now on, have Pite join the project.

397
00:23:47,080 --> 00:23:48,160
But if he screws anything up,

398
00:23:48,200 --> 00:23:49,160
it's on you.

399
00:23:49,520 --> 00:23:50,320
Understood.

400
00:23:53,000 --> 00:23:55,400
Keep sensitive documents more secure next time.

401
00:23:56,000 --> 00:23:57,080
If this happens again,

402
00:23:57,880 --> 00:23:59,200
don't bother coming back here.

403
00:24:00,480 --> 00:24:02,080
Understood. I'm sorry.

404
00:24:02,120 --> 00:24:02,960
You can go now.

405
00:24:05,000 --> 00:24:05,760
Okay.

406
00:24:20,920 --> 00:24:22,880
Dammit, I can't even have a smoke.

407
00:24:23,960 --> 00:24:24,920
Jeez.

408
00:24:29,280 --> 00:24:30,160
Hey.

409
00:24:30,200 --> 00:24:31,720
-P'Ing, hold on. -Hey.

410
00:24:33,240 --> 00:24:33,880
Hey.

411
00:24:36,920 --> 00:24:38,000
P'Ing, come on.

412
00:24:40,120 --> 00:24:40,880
You're dead.

413
00:24:42,120 --> 00:24:43,040
That's better.

414
00:24:43,080 --> 00:24:44,320
I went all day without smoking for you,

415
00:24:44,320 --> 00:24:46,200
and you're paying more attention to your game?

416
00:24:47,480 --> 00:24:49,400
Are you seriously jealous of a game?

417
00:24:52,880 --> 00:24:53,840
What game are you playing?

418
00:24:54,640 --> 00:24:56,280
Oh, this one?

419
00:24:56,600 --> 00:24:58,000
I've seen it on my feed.

420
00:24:58,800 --> 00:24:59,960
Shouldn't be that hard.

421
00:25:01,720 --> 00:25:02,680
Do you even know how to play?

422
00:25:03,320 --> 00:25:05,280
I can figure it out in one go.

423
00:25:05,480 --> 00:25:06,880
Want to bet I'll win?

424
00:25:07,960 --> 00:25:08,960
You're on.

425
00:25:09,320 --> 00:25:10,040
Bring it.

426
00:25:10,280 --> 00:25:11,520
You're going to lose.

427
00:25:11,560 --> 00:25:12,880
That's almost impossible.

428
00:25:14,600 --> 00:25:15,520
I'll take this character.

429
00:25:15,560 --> 00:25:17,080
It looks just as dumb as Pite.

430
00:25:17,080 --> 00:25:18,600
Now he wants to get in on...

431
00:25:18,640 --> 00:25:21,320
Director Pha-nu's condo units.

432
00:25:21,320 --> 00:25:22,840
I can't even turn him down.

433
00:25:22,840 --> 00:25:24,040
His mom asked me to let him in.

434
00:25:26,240 --> 00:25:27,160
P'Ing,

435
00:25:27,440 --> 00:25:29,440
I think Pite is nothing but trouble.

436
00:25:30,120 --> 00:25:32,800
Even with Itt watching over him, it's still a risk.

437
00:25:34,120 --> 00:25:35,960
Itt is younger.

438
00:25:36,240 --> 00:25:38,040
If Pite starts causing problems,

439
00:25:38,400 --> 00:25:39,560
will Itt even be able to handle him?

440
00:25:39,960 --> 00:25:41,280
He'll be just fine.

441
00:25:41,320 --> 00:25:44,640
Pite only needs to submit the documents as agreed,

442
00:25:44,640 --> 00:25:46,200
and Itt will handle the rest.

443
00:25:46,240 --> 00:25:48,200
As for right now, you just have to...

444
00:25:48,400 --> 00:25:52,760
wait for your doom in three, two, one.

445
00:25:53,000 --> 00:25:53,840
Done.

446
00:25:57,960 --> 00:25:59,040
I was just going easy on you.

447
00:25:59,040 --> 00:26:02,360
A noob will always be a noob, I guess.

448
00:26:02,400 --> 00:26:03,760
I was busy talking about Pite.

449
00:26:03,800 --> 00:26:05,320
Oh, really?

450
00:26:05,360 --> 00:26:06,800
So what? You still lost.

451
00:26:07,600 --> 00:26:08,960
Keep your promise.

452
00:26:08,960 --> 00:26:12,320
You have to go on a boat trip with me this Songkran.

453
00:26:13,200 --> 00:26:15,440
I can't, P'Ing. I have to go home.

454
00:26:15,480 --> 00:26:17,400
Jeez, what's the big deal?

455
00:26:17,720 --> 00:26:20,040
Afraid you won't win the Son of the Year award?

456
00:26:20,080 --> 00:26:22,040
If I don't go home this Songkran,

457
00:26:22,080 --> 00:26:24,720
I'll definitely be labeled an ungrateful son.

458
00:26:25,920 --> 00:26:27,480
Then just tell them that...

459
00:26:28,080 --> 00:26:30,680
you're being grateful right now

460
00:26:30,680 --> 00:26:32,080
by using your body

461
00:26:32,120 --> 00:26:34,280
to repay your mentor.

462
00:26:34,320 --> 00:26:35,040
Right?

463
00:26:35,240 --> 00:26:36,280
-Really? -Yeah.

464
00:26:39,200 --> 00:26:40,440
No, that tickles.

465
00:26:42,400 --> 00:26:43,160
P'Ing...

466
00:26:46,560 --> 00:26:47,360
Yok.

467
00:26:48,560 --> 00:26:49,320
Yok.

468
00:26:51,240 --> 00:26:52,560
Let's have a toast.

469
00:26:53,920 --> 00:26:56,080
Have a wonderful Songkran, everyone.

470
00:26:56,120 --> 00:26:57,600
You, too.

471
00:26:57,600 --> 00:26:58,800
-You, too. -Drink up.

472
00:27:03,640 --> 00:27:05,040
Ing is so good at his job,

473
00:27:05,440 --> 00:27:06,560
and Itt is doing great in school.

474
00:27:06,880 --> 00:27:08,480
He's won scholarships two years in a row.

475
00:27:09,120 --> 00:27:11,000
Having two fine sons like this,

476
00:27:11,320 --> 00:27:13,520
I could die today with no regrets.

477
00:27:13,920 --> 00:27:14,720
Isn't that right?

478
00:27:14,800 --> 00:27:15,840
-Absolutely. -Right.

479
00:27:15,880 --> 00:27:17,440
-A toast to the two of them. -Congratulations.

480
00:27:17,440 --> 00:27:19,520
-A toast to your nephews. -Cheers.

481
00:27:26,800 --> 00:27:27,480
P'Ing.

482
00:27:28,640 --> 00:27:29,800
You've had enough.

483
00:27:30,280 --> 00:27:31,560
Let me take you to your room.

484
00:27:31,600 --> 00:27:33,560
Ing, go take a quick nap upstairs

485
00:27:33,600 --> 00:27:35,360
and come back for another round later.

486
00:27:35,440 --> 00:27:36,880
It's only just past 9 p.m.

487
00:27:37,160 --> 00:27:39,480
I'll take him up to rest now.

488
00:27:39,920 --> 00:27:41,680
Okay. Take good care of your brother.

489
00:27:43,200 --> 00:27:44,840
Hold him steady.

490
00:27:49,320 --> 00:27:50,400
-Come on. -Alright.

491
00:27:51,280 --> 00:27:52,360
Watch out.

492
00:27:55,800 --> 00:27:56,520
P'Ing,

493
00:27:56,800 --> 00:27:58,600
Auntie Aoi said your room isn't ready yet.

494
00:27:58,920 --> 00:28:00,200
You can sleep in my room for now.

495
00:28:13,200 --> 00:28:14,280
Itt,

496
00:28:14,280 --> 00:28:15,880
the money you got today...

497
00:28:16,720 --> 00:28:18,200
Don't waste it, okay?

498
00:28:19,000 --> 00:28:21,200
You're grown up. Start getting something of your own.

499
00:28:21,960 --> 00:28:23,040
Don't worry.

500
00:28:26,840 --> 00:28:28,560
So, how's the condo project going?

501
00:28:29,920 --> 00:28:31,080
Everything is on hold for now,

502
00:28:31,720 --> 00:28:33,800
but I'll get it all sorted out after Songkran.

503
00:28:33,800 --> 00:28:35,160
There aren't any issues at the moment.

504
00:28:36,400 --> 00:28:37,680
What about Pite?

505
00:28:38,280 --> 00:28:40,040
Has he been causing any trouble?

506
00:28:42,600 --> 00:28:43,840
He listens to me just fine.

507
00:28:44,320 --> 00:28:45,920
Keep a close eye on him.

508
00:28:46,640 --> 00:28:48,160
Let me know if anything happens.

509
00:28:50,400 --> 00:28:51,160
Will do.

510
00:28:51,800 --> 00:28:52,680
Now, go on.

511
00:28:53,680 --> 00:28:55,680
Just go away. I want to sleep now.

512
00:28:57,920 --> 00:28:58,720
Okay.

513
00:29:11,840 --> 00:29:12,760
P'Ing...

514
00:29:26,640 --> 00:29:30,040
It's been so long since I've seen you fall asleep.

515
00:29:35,120 --> 00:29:36,600
Your lips are so soft,

516
00:29:37,400 --> 00:29:40,520
but how come you never say anything nice to me?

517
00:30:06,760 --> 00:30:07,560
Yok...

518
00:31:00,080 --> 00:31:00,840
Oh...

519
00:31:02,560 --> 00:31:03,200
Hey.

520
00:31:03,880 --> 00:31:04,800
What a coincidence.

521
00:31:05,760 --> 00:31:06,520
Hold on.

522
00:31:07,080 --> 00:31:08,120
What's with the rush?

523
00:31:08,840 --> 00:31:10,080
I just got some money.

524
00:31:11,600 --> 00:31:13,080
Come on, my treat.

525
00:31:14,800 --> 00:31:15,680
Come on.

526
00:31:34,920 --> 00:31:35,680
What are you doing?

527
00:32:01,800 --> 00:32:02,560
Open up.

528
00:32:11,240 --> 00:32:12,920
Let's go sit down over there.

529
00:32:25,160 --> 00:32:26,440
What brings you to Bangkok?

530
00:32:27,240 --> 00:32:28,440
I'm always here.

531
00:32:29,720 --> 00:32:30,640
I went to Pattaya

532
00:32:31,040 --> 00:32:32,320
on a trip with my client.

533
00:32:32,640 --> 00:32:33,440
What about you?

534
00:32:34,680 --> 00:32:36,440
Why are you all alone on Songkran?

535
00:32:40,440 --> 00:32:43,080
Last time, you were stealing candy.

536
00:32:43,200 --> 00:32:44,400
What are you up to this time?

537
00:32:49,200 --> 00:32:51,920
Next time, if you want some candy,

538
00:32:52,720 --> 00:32:53,640
just buy it.

539
00:32:54,880 --> 00:32:56,120
Don't do that kind of thing again.

540
00:32:56,240 --> 00:32:57,360
What right do you have to lecture me?

541
00:32:58,320 --> 00:32:59,320
Look,

542
00:33:00,600 --> 00:33:02,280
you always take someone's good intentions

543
00:33:02,320 --> 00:33:03,400
as a lecture, don't you?

544
00:33:13,040 --> 00:33:15,600
Lock on. That's our target.

545
00:33:16,040 --> 00:33:18,120
Happy Songkran My name is Force.

546
00:33:18,600 --> 00:33:20,000
See you

547
00:33:24,360 --> 00:33:25,600
I was sleeping so soundly

548
00:33:25,640 --> 00:33:26,760
I forgot to call Yok.

549
00:33:27,280 --> 00:33:29,440
Anyway, why hasn't he called me yet?

550
00:33:31,560 --> 00:33:32,360
Oh, here it is.

551
00:33:33,240 --> 00:33:34,040
[My Capy: Happy Songkran Day.]

552
00:33:34,120 --> 00:33:35,080
[May you always be happy]

553
00:33:35,080 --> 00:33:35,640
[and prosperous.]

554
00:33:35,680 --> 00:33:37,600
"Happy Songkran.

555
00:33:37,920 --> 00:33:42,080
May you always be happy and prosperous."

556
00:33:44,440 --> 00:33:47,360
Isn't this the kind of message you send to your parents?

557
00:33:52,280 --> 00:33:53,080
Hello?

558
00:33:54,240 --> 00:33:56,240
Hello. You're up already?

559
00:33:57,000 --> 00:33:59,480
Yeah. Why didn't you call me last night?

560
00:33:59,840 --> 00:34:01,120
Well, I called Itt last night.

561
00:34:01,280 --> 00:34:03,440
He said you'd passed out drunk,

562
00:34:03,560 --> 00:34:04,960
so I didn't call.

563
00:34:07,320 --> 00:34:08,440
Next time, just call me.

564
00:34:08,440 --> 00:34:10,159
Why would you even call Itt?

565
00:34:10,199 --> 00:34:11,080
I'm not dead yet.

566
00:34:11,120 --> 00:34:12,679
Why leave a message with him?

567
00:34:13,159 --> 00:34:14,920
Are you still not sober yet?

568
00:34:16,000 --> 00:34:17,920
I'm sober now, thanks to your message.

569
00:34:18,679 --> 00:34:20,639
What kind of message were you expecting?

570
00:34:22,920 --> 00:34:23,920
I'm done talking to you.

571
00:34:23,960 --> 00:34:24,880
You're annoying.

572
00:34:29,840 --> 00:34:31,239
-Hey, Ing. -I shouldn't have called him.

573
00:34:31,280 --> 00:34:32,159
You're up now?

574
00:34:33,159 --> 00:34:34,400
I have something to ask you.

575
00:34:37,639 --> 00:34:38,560
Yes, Dad.

576
00:34:39,600 --> 00:34:41,280
When are you going to visit Grandpa?

577
00:34:42,520 --> 00:34:44,000
I'm planning to see...

578
00:34:45,560 --> 00:34:46,800
Mom's relatives tomorrow,

579
00:34:46,800 --> 00:34:48,480
then I'll head to Grandpa's in two days.

580
00:34:48,520 --> 00:34:50,560
Are you bringing your brother along?

581
00:34:52,400 --> 00:34:53,159
Are you coming?

582
00:34:53,440 --> 00:34:54,120
I'd love to.

583
00:34:54,159 --> 00:34:55,639
I haven't seen Grandpa in ages.

584
00:34:57,280 --> 00:34:58,600
You've grown up, haven't you?

585
00:35:01,560 --> 00:35:02,280
Right,

586
00:35:02,400 --> 00:35:06,680
I'm thinking of taking Itt to see the Sukonsiris as well.

587
00:35:07,040 --> 00:35:08,720
Oh, that's even better.

588
00:35:09,280 --> 00:35:10,320
It'd be good for you two

589
00:35:10,320 --> 00:35:12,320
to get to know their kids.

590
00:35:13,520 --> 00:35:14,360
In that case,

591
00:35:14,360 --> 00:35:15,880
could you let Uncle Pongpaisan know

592
00:35:15,880 --> 00:35:17,160
that I'll be bringing Itt along?

593
00:35:17,960 --> 00:35:19,600
Sure, I'll give him a call.

594
00:35:24,600 --> 00:35:26,160
I'm coming for you, Yok.

595
00:35:29,280 --> 00:35:30,240
Thank you.

596
00:35:30,280 --> 00:35:31,680
Please enjoy your meal.

597
00:35:32,400 --> 00:35:33,560
I see.

598
00:35:34,720 --> 00:35:37,280
So this is khao chae, the royal Thai dish?

599
00:35:38,800 --> 00:35:39,720
I've never seen it before.

600
00:35:39,760 --> 00:35:41,600
This is my first time getting to try it.

601
00:35:42,080 --> 00:35:43,280
Well, we make this ourselves

602
00:35:43,280 --> 00:35:44,400
every Songkran.

603
00:35:44,440 --> 00:35:46,120
It's an heirloom recipe from my great-grandmother.

604
00:35:46,640 --> 00:35:48,080
You'll fall in love with it once you try it.

605
00:35:48,120 --> 00:35:49,280
How are we supposed to eat it?

606
00:35:49,360 --> 00:35:51,680
Eat the side dishes first to awaken your taste buds.

607
00:35:52,000 --> 00:35:53,320
Then eat the rice.

608
00:35:53,880 --> 00:35:55,680
Don't mix the sides into the rice, though.

609
00:35:56,480 --> 00:35:57,640
Go ahead and try it.

610
00:36:03,040 --> 00:36:04,360
It smells so good, and it's delicious.

611
00:36:04,360 --> 00:36:05,200
I'm not surprised

612
00:36:05,240 --> 00:36:06,920
that you like it so much.

613
00:36:07,040 --> 00:36:08,680
I'm starting to get hooked on it myself.

614
00:36:09,000 --> 00:36:10,160
If you like it that much,

615
00:36:10,320 --> 00:36:11,680
come join us again next Songkran.

616
00:36:11,720 --> 00:36:12,920
Oh, I'd love to.

617
00:36:13,200 --> 00:36:14,000
You're always welcome.

618
00:36:14,000 --> 00:36:15,800
Oh, I almost forgot to ask.

619
00:36:15,800 --> 00:36:18,160
Itt gave you the report on the land survey

620
00:36:18,200 --> 00:36:19,640
in Pattaya already, right?

621
00:36:20,080 --> 00:36:21,080
Yes, he did.

622
00:36:21,120 --> 00:36:22,920
The company mentioned that the plot of land

623
00:36:22,920 --> 00:36:23,920
is in an excellent location.

624
00:36:23,920 --> 00:36:26,280
So, what stage are we at now?

625
00:36:26,400 --> 00:36:28,240
We're currently working on the draft.

626
00:36:28,240 --> 00:36:29,880
I'll send it to you as soon as it's ready.

627
00:36:30,000 --> 00:36:31,880
Please let me know once it's done.

628
00:36:31,920 --> 00:36:33,160
I'll get the next steps moving right away.

629
00:36:33,520 --> 00:36:35,600
I'm sure everything will go quite smoothly.

630
00:36:35,600 --> 00:36:36,680
Absolutely.

631
00:36:36,680 --> 00:36:38,920
May I oversee this project?

632
00:36:45,240 --> 00:36:46,520
That sounds like a great idea, Mr. Phet.

633
00:36:47,360 --> 00:36:48,520
Yok is your brother,

634
00:36:48,560 --> 00:36:49,480
and he's working with me.

635
00:36:49,480 --> 00:36:50,600
So I can just pass messages

636
00:36:50,600 --> 00:36:51,400
to you through him.

637
00:36:51,440 --> 00:36:52,440
That'll make things easier.

638
00:36:53,320 --> 00:36:55,360
Sounds good. Let's go with that.

639
00:36:56,760 --> 00:36:58,600
We've got some desserts, too.

640
00:36:58,640 --> 00:36:59,520
I'll go get them.

641
00:37:00,000 --> 00:37:00,800
Thank you.

642
00:37:05,160 --> 00:37:07,360
Itt, have you bought that new game yet?

643
00:37:07,400 --> 00:37:08,320
Which one?

644
00:37:08,480 --> 00:37:10,080
I've been busy with the work P'Ing gave me,

645
00:37:10,120 --> 00:37:11,160
so I haven't had the time.

646
00:37:12,480 --> 00:37:13,360
All you do is work.

647
00:37:13,400 --> 00:37:14,920
Songkran is a long holiday, isn't it?

648
00:37:15,280 --> 00:37:16,320
Let's play together sometime.

649
00:37:17,600 --> 00:37:19,000
Gaming strains your eyes.

650
00:37:19,120 --> 00:37:20,200
You shouldn't play anymore.

651
00:37:23,960 --> 00:37:25,320
Your eyes get tired from working, too.

652
00:37:38,120 --> 00:37:38,920
Here it is.

653
00:37:45,280 --> 00:37:46,360
Thank you very much.

654
00:37:50,120 --> 00:37:51,760
Yok, what's wrong?

655
00:37:51,800 --> 00:37:52,920
You're all hunched over.

656
00:37:54,920 --> 00:37:56,080
I think I'm getting a cramp.

657
00:37:56,520 --> 00:37:57,720
Have you been overtraining in boxing?

658
00:37:57,920 --> 00:37:59,200
Take better care of yourself.

659
00:37:59,880 --> 00:38:00,480
I will.

660
00:38:16,400 --> 00:38:18,400
Thank you so much for the khao chae.

661
00:38:18,400 --> 00:38:19,720
It was quite a new experience.

662
00:38:19,760 --> 00:38:20,600
My pleasure.

663
00:38:20,600 --> 00:38:22,560
I'm sorry if I wasn't the best host.

664
00:38:23,880 --> 00:38:24,840
Excuse me.

665
00:38:27,440 --> 00:38:29,120
Yok, I'll leave them in your hands.

666
00:38:30,080 --> 00:38:31,320
-Got it. -Excuse me.

667
00:38:34,720 --> 00:38:35,920
Itt, come here.

668
00:38:39,800 --> 00:38:40,520
Get in.

669
00:38:42,600 --> 00:38:43,640
Get in the car.

670
00:39:07,320 --> 00:39:08,200
What are you doing?

671
00:39:11,200 --> 00:39:12,120
No, what are you doing?

672
00:39:12,400 --> 00:39:13,560
We haven't seen each other for days,

673
00:39:13,600 --> 00:39:14,920
not even during Songkran.

674
00:39:15,000 --> 00:39:16,920
What's with that message you sent?

675
00:39:16,960 --> 00:39:18,240
Was that meant for your parents?

676
00:39:18,280 --> 00:39:19,200
Now that I'm finally here,

677
00:39:19,240 --> 00:39:20,800
you're acting all disgusted.

678
00:39:20,800 --> 00:39:22,040
Do I look that disgusting?

679
00:39:23,040 --> 00:39:23,800
P'Ing,

680
00:39:24,080 --> 00:39:25,400
do we have to talk about it now?

681
00:39:26,040 --> 00:39:27,000
Someone might see us.

682
00:39:28,160 --> 00:39:29,000
Fine.

683
00:39:31,320 --> 00:39:33,560
If you're that afraid, we can talk later.

684
00:39:48,440 --> 00:39:49,440
Let's go.

685
00:40:11,480 --> 00:40:12,600
[Yok]

686
00:40:22,320 --> 00:40:23,200
Hello?

687
00:40:24,800 --> 00:40:26,080
Were you sleeping?

688
00:40:27,680 --> 00:40:29,160
Well, I was going to.

689
00:40:31,320 --> 00:40:32,640
It's not even midnight yet.

690
00:40:32,960 --> 00:40:34,440
You never go to bed this early.

691
00:40:36,160 --> 00:40:38,320
I'm visiting my grandpa tomorrow morning.

692
00:40:38,600 --> 00:40:39,680
Oh...

693
00:40:41,240 --> 00:40:42,240
Is something up?

694
00:40:44,600 --> 00:40:46,400
I was thinking we could go out tomorrow.

695
00:40:49,520 --> 00:40:52,160
We just saw each other. You miss me already?

696
00:40:56,240 --> 00:40:57,560
If you're not available, it's okay.

697
00:40:57,640 --> 00:40:59,080
We can meet after you get back.

698
00:40:59,080 --> 00:41:00,080
Wait, hold on.

699
00:41:01,400 --> 00:41:03,360
You can come to my condo now.

700
00:41:04,720 --> 00:41:05,680
Right now?

701
00:41:05,840 --> 00:41:06,640
Yeah.

702
00:41:07,000 --> 00:41:07,760
Alright.

703
00:41:08,160 --> 00:41:09,280
But you'll have to wait.

704
00:41:09,640 --> 00:41:11,360
I can't leave until my family's gone to bed.

705
00:41:11,600 --> 00:41:12,400
Okay.

706
00:42:57,640 --> 00:42:59,160
Have you ever thought about me?

707
00:42:59,560 --> 00:43:00,400
You can do whatever you want,

708
00:43:00,400 --> 00:43:01,840
but I can't.

709
00:43:03,400 --> 00:43:04,040
Fight.

710
00:43:04,040 --> 00:43:04,080
Fight.

711
00:43:04,680 --> 00:43:06,120
You don't know anything

712
00:43:06,600 --> 00:43:06,640
about us or my training.

713
00:43:06,640 --> 00:43:07,600
about us or my training.

714
00:43:07,600 --> 00:43:07,800
about us or my training.

715
00:43:09,160 --> 00:43:09,840
Whoa...

716
00:43:09,840 --> 00:43:09,960
Whoa...

717
00:43:12,080 --> 00:43:12,840
Yeah.

718
00:43:19,080 --> 00:43:20,320
I trusted you with this.

719
00:43:20,320 --> 00:43:21,600
What the hell have you done?

720
00:43:22,120 --> 00:43:23,920
P'Ing, I didn't do it.
